## Context

Tracker [[1703]], document 4. Today only in [[1500]], [[1506]], [[1508]],
[[1509]]. This is the document M2 code is built from, so it comes first among
the missing ones.

## Author constraints (2026-09-30, interactive)

- "What we are working towards is a complete system specification. The idea
  is to write it explicit and review the heck out of it before we launch
  extraction."
- "We want something that works first, then M4 will polish."
- "Pragmatic programmer, results-oriented over theoretical purity."
- Conceptual documents name no storage and no presentation (rule set for
  `docs/jetp-fusion.md`, ticket 1701).

So every rule in a spec document carries the milestone that needs it (M2,
M3a, M3b, M4, or later). The M2 and M3 slice is the minimum that produces
correct, traceable results; everything else is tagged M4 or later and is not
built before it.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `docs/jetp-extraction.md`, conceptual, covers document deduplication before reading, text layers per format, parsers per repeated series, assisted reading with row-by-row review for one-offs, dispositions with reasons, dated snapshots and restatements, replay and idempotence, red tests per extractor
- [x] Every rule carries its milestone; the M2 slice is the minimum that extracts all held documents correctly and traceably
- [ ] [[1500]] and [[1506]] exit criteria are consistent with it
